<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">Lesson Planner – Theme # What Is Sustainable Fashion? – Lesson # 1</h2>
<p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <tr>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</p></td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 10th Grade (CEFR: B1.1)</p></td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Sustainable Fashion</p></td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> What Is Sustainable Fashion?</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td colspan="3" style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Show comprehension of extended speeches on familiar topics. Interactive: Organize information from group discussions.</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can summarize the main points from a talk on sustainable fashion trends (e.g., "The main points were on using organic cotton and recycled fabrics as eco-friendly materials in fashion.")<br>Can organize key ideas from a group discussion about current and past fashion trends by taking notes and summarizing (e.g., "In the 1970s, bright colors and patterns were popular, while today's fashion emphasizes neutral tones and sustainability.")<br>Can understand and relay ideas from an extended speech on fashion industry changes (e.g., "Fashion will have to become more sustainable and focus on using recyclable materials").</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</i></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by playing a short audio clip (30-45 seconds) featuring sounds of a bustling fashion show (music, applause, faint announcer) and then transitions to sounds of nature (birds, water). Students listen and reflect on the contrast. The teacher asks, "What did you hear? What did these sounds make you think about?"</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher introduces the concept of "sustainable fashion" by showing pictures of garments made from recycled materials versus fast fashion items. The teacher explicitly models the pronunciation of key vocabulary for the lesson: "sustainable" (stress on the second syllable, /səˈsteɪnəbl/), "fashionable" (stress on the first syllable, /ˈfæʃənəbl/), "eco-friendly" (stress on "eco," /ˈiːkoʊ ˌfrendli/), "vintage" (/ˈvɪntɪdʒ/, focusing on /v/ sound), and "wear" (/wɛr/, focusing on /w/ sound). The teacher explains that sustainable fashion focuses on protecting the "environment" by using "recycled materials."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is 'sustainable fashion' about buying clothes every week?" (Expected answer: No, it's about making thoughtful choices.)</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If a shirt is made from 'recycled materials,' is it good for the 'environment'?" (Expected answer: Yes, it is 'eco-friendly'.)</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Sustainable Fashion".</i></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Students listen to a short audio clip (approx. 2-3 minutes) from a podcast or a news report titled "The Rise of Sustainable Fashion." The audio provides an overview of what sustainable fashion is, mentions "brands" that are adopting "eco-friendly" practices, and briefly discusses how "fashion trends will continue to evolve" towards sustainability. It touches upon using "vintage" items and "recycled materials."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening: Understanding global meaning of short and simple audio messages.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Listening:</b> Students listen to the audio once and answer: "What is the main topic of this podcast/report?" (Expected answer: Sustainable fashion and its importance).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False Activity:</b> Students listen again and decide if the following statements are True or False based on the audio:
            <ul>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Sustainable fashion only uses new, expensive 'materials'." (False)</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Many 'brands' are trying to be more 'eco-friendly'." (True)</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Buying 'vintage' clothes is a way to be 'sustainable'." (True)</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Accuracy focus on Listening.</i></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice listening for specific vocabulary (nouns: *fashion, trend, vintage, retro, materials, sustainability, industry, environment, prediction*; verbs: *evolve, predict, adopt, reflect, recycle*; adjectives: *sustainable, fashionable, trendy, eco-friendly, recycled*) and grammatical structures (Past continuous with present simple to compare trends, Past perfect for completed actions, Future simple for predictions).</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Gap-fill Listening (Controlled Practice):</b> The teacher provides a transcript of a section of the audio with key vocabulary words (e.g., *sustainability, eco-friendly, recycled, evolve, vintage, trend*) removed. Students listen to the audio clip again (focused listening on specific sentences) and fill in the missing words. For example: "The 'fashion' _________ will continue to _________ towards using more _________ and _________ 'materials'."</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Identifying Grammar in Context (Semi-controlled):</b> The teacher plays specific sentences from the audio twice. Students identify and write down sentences that use:
            <ul>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Past continuous with present simple (e.g., "In the 1990s, designers were introducing bold colors, but today's 'fashion' emphasizes 'sustainability'").</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Future simple for predictions (e.g., "Experts 'predict' that 'fashion trends will continue to evolve' towards 'eco-friendly' practices.").</li>
            </ul>
            After listening, students share their identified sentences and discuss the meaning.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Peer-Check and Vocabulary Match:</b> Students work in pairs. The teacher provides a list of the 8-10 target vocabulary words from the audio (e.g., *sustainable, fashion, trend, vintage, eco-friendly, recycle, materials, industry, environment, prediction*). Each pair receives cards with definitions or synonyms. They listen to the audio one more time, focusing on how these words are used, and then match the words to their correct definitions. They peer-check their answers, discussing any discrepancies based on their listening comprehension.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Sustainable Fashion".</i></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format: Listening for Group Discussion and Summary</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students are divided into small groups (3-4 students). They listen to a slightly longer audio segment (approx. 3-4 minutes) which includes a discussion or an interview about "fashion industry changes" and different perspectives on "sustainability" in "fashion." This audio will explicitly use the target grammar (Past continuous with present simple for comparison, Past perfect for context, Future simple for predictions) and vocabulary (e.g., 'fast fashion is cheap and convenient,' while others describe it as 'harmful and wasteful,' showing how language reflects different values about sustainability). As they listen, each group member takes notes on key ideas, examples of 'sustainable practices,' and 'eco-friendly materials' mentioned, and any 'predictions' about the future of 'fashion'.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">After listening, groups collaborate to organize their notes and orally summarize the main points of the discussion. They should also compare past and present trends discussed, using phrases like "In the 1970s, people were wearing bright colors, but now fashion emphasizes neutral tones and 'sustainability'." One student from each group shares their summary with the class. This activity encourages them to "organize information from group discussions" based on what they've heard.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Formative assessment strategy.</i></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during group summary presentation, focusing on listening comprehension and note-taking effectiveness.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group orally presents a 1-minute summary of the main points from the audio discussion. They must demonstrate their ability to "summarize the main points from a talk on sustainable fashion trends" and "organize key ideas from a group discussion."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Clear articulation of words, especially target vocabulary like "sustainable," "eco-friendly," "vintage."</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> Integration of at least 5-7 new vocabulary words from the lesson (e.g., *sustainable, fashion, trend, vintage, eco-friendly, recycled, materials, industry, environment, prediction*).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and Accuracy of Summary:</b> Main points from the audio are correctly identified and presented.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration and Organization:</b> Group members effectively share information and present a coherent summary.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar Application:</b> Attempts to use Past continuous/Present simple and Future simple for comparisons/predictions heard in the audio.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a quick exit ticket:
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one new thing you learned about 'sustainable fashion' from today's listening activities?"</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Which vocabulary word was the most challenging to understand in context, and why?"</li>
        </ul></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did listening to different audio inputs help you understand 'What Is Sustainable Fashion' today?"</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can you apply the concept of 'sustainable fashion' to your own clothing choices or discussions about the 'environment'?"</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The listening activities successfully introduced the core vocabulary and the concept of sustainable fashion. Students demonstrated good comprehension of main ideas and some details. The pronunciation practice for /v/ and /w/ and word stress will need continued reinforcement. Some students found it challenging to quickly identify specific grammar structures while listening; more targeted practice with sentence fragments might be beneficial. The group summaries were generally clear, and students attempted to use the new vocabulary, showing that the input was accessible for B1.1 level.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 2, students will further explore the theme "What Is Sustainable Fashion?" through reading comprehension activities. They will read a text that incorporates the same target vocabulary and grammar, allowing them to see the words in a different context and deepen their understanding of the topic before actively producing the language.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ min</p></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>